Gemma-3:
Let A be the given matrix:
A = \begin{bmatrix} 4 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\ -1 & 5 & 1 & -1 \\ -5 & 0 & -4 & 2 \\ -1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \end{bmatrix}

We can compute the determinant of A by cofactor expansion along the last row.
det(A) = (-1) * C_{41} + (-1) * C_{42} + 0 * C_{43} + 0 * C_{44}
= (-1) * C_{41} + (-1) * C_{42}

C_{41} is the cofactor of the element in the 4th row and 1st column.
C_{41} = (-1)^{4+1} * M_{41} = (-1)^5 * M_{41} = -M_{41}
M_{41} is the determinant of the 3x3 matrix obtained by removing the 4th row and 1st column:
M_{41} = \begin{vmatrix} 4 & -2 & 5 \\ 5 & 1 & -1 \\ 0 & -4 & 2 \end{vmatrix}
= 4 * \begin{vmatrix} 1 & -1 \\ -4 & 2 \end{vmatrix} - (-2) * \begin{vmatrix} 5 & -1 \\ 0 & 2 \end{vmatrix} + 5 * \begin{vmatrix} 5 & 1 \\ 0 & -4 \end{vmatrix}
= 4 * (1*2 - (-1)*(-4)) + 2 * (5*2 - (-1)*0) + 5 * (5*(-4) - 1*0)
= 4 * (2 - 4) + 2 * (10 - 0) + 5 * (-20 - 0)
= 4 * (-2) + 2 * 10 + 5 * (-20)
= -8 + 20 - 100
= -88

C_{42} is the cofactor of the element in the 4th row and 2nd column.
C_{42} = (-1)^{4+2} * M_{42} = 1 * M_{42} = M_{42}
M_{42} is the determinant of the 3x3 matrix obtained by removing the 4th row and 2nd column:
M_{42} = \begin{vmatrix} 4 & -2 & 5 \\ -1 & 1 & -1 \\ -5 & -4 & 2 \end{vmatrix}
= 4 * \begin{vmatrix} 1 & -1 \\ -4 & 2 \end{vmatrix} - (-2) * \begin{vmatrix} -1 & -1 \\ -5 & 2 \end{vmatrix} + 5 * \begin{vmatrix} -1 & 1 \\ -5 & -4 \end{vmatrix}
= 4 * (1*2 - (-1)*(-4)) + 2 * ((-1)*2 - (-1)*(-5)) + 5 * ((-1)*(-4) - 1*(-5))
= 4 * (2 - 4) + 2 * (-2 - 5) + 5 * (4 + 5)
= 4 * (-2) + 2 * (-7) + 5 * 9
= -8 - 14 + 45
= 23

det(A) = (-1) * C_{41} + (-1) * C_{42}
= (-1) * (-88) + (-1) * (23)
= 88 - 23
= 65

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{65}$
